#kaocha/v1
;; TWO SUITES, ONE TREE. What separates them is a ^:integration on the deftest,
;; not a directory — a namespace is free to hold both kinds, and here most will:
;; the shape's construction checks are unit, drawing it is integration, and they
;; belong next to each other.
;;
;; :unit is our own logic with nothing outside this process — no database, no
;; socket, no clock worth waiting on. Generative tests are the unit suite here,
;; not an extra, which is why test.check is in :deps rather than :dev. Meant to
;; be run on every save.
;;
;; :integration opens real things: a datahike store on disk, manifold streams,
;; and anything that shells out to graphviz to render a graph. It is the gate
;; BEFORE A COMMIT, and it is not in the fast loop.
;;
;; The runner is `clojure -M:dev:test <suite>` — kaocha lives in the :dev alias
;; and the main-opts in :test, so :test alone has no kaocha on the classpath.
{:tests
 [{:id           :unit
   :test-paths   ["test"]
   :source-paths ["src"]
   :kaocha.filter/skip-meta [:integration]}

  {:id           :integration
   :test-paths   ["test"]
   :source-paths ["src"]
   :kaocha.filter/focus-meta [:integration]}]

 :kaocha/reporter [kaocha.report/dots]
 :kaocha.plugin/capture-output true}
